IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-vintage`

-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 25 September 2024.
-- LAYER 1: the First, Second and Third Schedules (the Fourth Schedule is in sgba-p1-online.l4, with ss 2A to 2D).
-- The First and Second Schedules decide what "broadcasting apparatus" and "licensable broadcasting service" are,
-- so the decision functions here take the date as an input and answer NOTHING outside the window in which the
-- deposited text is the text in force (sgba-vintage.l4). No past text of either Schedule was obtained.
-- (The legislative history at BA1994.txt:4645-4648 lists G.N. S 549/2012 "Amendment of First Schedule"; its text
-- was not obtained, so nothing here says what the First Schedule listed before the deposited text.)

§ `First Schedule -- broadcasting apparatus`

-- src:4347 | 1. Television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system).
@ref First Schedule, item 1 (src:4347)
-- src:4354 | In this Schedule, “television receive-only satellite receiving system” means
-- src:4355 | any apparatus (including a dish antenna) or any combination of apparatus capable
-- src:4356 | of direct reception of any broadcasting service emitted from or passing through
-- src:4357 | any communication or broadcast satellite in extraterrestrial space.
@ref First Schedule, interpretation paragraph (src:4354-4357)
GIVEN a IS A Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an apparatus is a television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)` MEANS
    a's `capable of direct reception from a satellite`

-- The First Schedule lists exactly one item. A date outside the window of the deposited text answers NOTHING.
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      a IS A Apparatus
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the apparatus is specified in the First Schedule on` MEANS
    IF `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`an apparatus is a television receive-only satellite receiving system (TVRO system)` a)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Second Schedule -- licensable broadcasting services`

-- src:4364 | 1. Free-to-air nationwide television services.
-- src:4365 | 2. Free-to-air localised television services.
-- src:4366 | 3. Free-to-air international television services.
-- src:4367 | 4. Subscription nationwide television services.
-- src:4368 | 5. Subscription localised television services.
-- src:4369 | 6. Subscription international television services.
-- src:4370 | 7. Special interest television services.
-- src:4371 | 8. Free-to-air nationwide radio services.
-- src:4372 | 9. Free-to-air localised radio services.
-- src:4373 | 10. Free-to-air international radio services.
-- src:4374 | 11. Subscription nationwide radio services.
-- src:4375 | 12. Subscription localised radio services.
-- src:4376 | 13. Subscription international radio services.
-- src:4377 | 14. Special interest radio services.
-- src:4378 | 15. Audiotext services.
-- src:4379 | 16. Videotext services.
-- src:4380 | 17. Teletext services.
-- src:4381 | 18. Video-on-demand services.
-- src:4382 | 19. Broadcast data services.
-- src:4383 | 20. Computer online services.
@ref Second Schedule, items 1 to 20 (src:4364-4383)
GIVEN s IS A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST x THEN TRUE

-- src:4384 | For the purposes of this Schedule, a delivery system is not to be deemed to be a
-- src:4385 | licensable broadcasting service by reason only that facilities or expertise are
-- src:4386 | provided for the delivery of any broadcasting service.
@ref Second Schedule, closing paragraph (src:4384-4386)
-- The paragraph says what does NOT make a delivery system a licensable broadcasting service.
-- NOTHING means the paragraph does not speak (the delivery system does something else as well).
GIVEN `facilities or expertise are provided for the delivery of a broadcasting service, and nothing more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the delivery system is deemed a licensable broadcasting service by reason only of providing facilities or expertise for delivery` MEANS
    IF `facilities or expertise are provided for the delivery of a broadcasting service, and nothing more` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      s IS A MAYBE `Second Schedule service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the service is specified in the Second Schedule on` MEANS
    IF `the deposited text of the Act is the text in force on` d
    THEN JUST (`the service is one of the twenty items of the Second Schedule` s)
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Third Schedule -- relevant licensable broadcasting service`

-- src:4397 | First column Second column
-- src:4398 | Provider
-- src:4399 | Licensable broadcasting service
-- src:4400 | (a) StarHub Cable Vision Ltd.
-- src:4401 | 1. Subscription nationwide television
-- src:4402 | service (b) SingNet Pte. Ltd.
@ref Third Schedule, row 1 (src:4397-4402)
GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is named in the Third Schedule as a provider of a subscription nationwide television service` MEANS
    name EQUALS "StarHub Cable Vision Ltd." OR name EQUALS "SingNet Pte. Ltd."
